{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgTwnC4iZSr2iRr5FCDLzM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T34 — Phase 5 — Working memory state model + working_memory_checkpoints table\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 5\n4\t**Type:** backend\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** R33\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task delivers the per-task, short-lived working-memory state model the spec mandates in §5 — making context management explicit instead of implicit prompt accumulation — and pins it to a versioned `working_memory_checkpoints` SQLite table so checkpoints can be restored. The state model contains exactly the eleven fields the spec enumerates; the checkpoint schema preserves the full state along with timestamps and a checkpoint name so T35's `checkpoint` operation has a target to write into and T37's restore tests have a target to restore from.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Working memory is per-task and short-lived. It should be explicit rather than implicit prompt accumulation. Working memory contains: task statement; interpreted intent; active files and symbols; active hypotheses; active failures; current plan; selected memories; excluded memories and reasons; budget decisions; unresolved questions; verification status.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n17\t\n18\t> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: explicit per-task working memory state; operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint; MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context; tests for token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n19\t\n20\t> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n21\t\n22\t## Inputs\n23\t\n24\t- Dependency outputs:\n25\t  - R33 verdict — Phase 4 retrieval is complete; `RetrievalBundle` / `BundleResult` are stable and can be embedded under `selected_memories`/`excluded_memories`.\n26\t  - T27 `IntentClassification` — populates `interpreted_intent`.\n27\t  - T28 `ResolvedAnchor` set — populates `active_files_and_symbols` seeds.\n28\t  - T31 `RetrievalBundle` — supplies `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories` (with reasons) verbatim per the Phase 4 forward-compatibility contract.\n29\t- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n30\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — SQLite connection conventions, migration helpers.\n31\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — for the `verification_status` enum reused under \"verification status\".\n32\t  - Phase 1 identity (`IdentityResolver`) — every reference inside working memory uses a stable identity.\n33\t- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, schema parity); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references; project build commands).\n34\t\n35\t## Steps\n36\t\n37\t1. Re-read spec §5. Working Memory and §Phase 5: Working Memory in full; copy the eleven-field state list verbatim into a doc comment at the top of `state.rs`.\n38\t2. Create the module skeleton: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs` re-exports `state`, `operations` (T35), `event_hooks` (T36) and registers the module with `lib.rs`.\n39\t3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` with `WorkingMemoryState { task_statement: String, interpreted_intent: IntentClassification, active_files: BTreeSet<FileIdentity>, active_symbols: BTreeSet<SymbolIdentity>, active_hypotheses: Vec<Hypothesis>, active_failures: Vec<FailureRecord>, current_plan: Option<PlanRef>, selected_memories: Vec<BundleResult>, excluded_memories: Vec<ExcludedMemory>, budget_decisions: BudgetDecisions, unresolved_questions: Vec<String>, verification_status: WorkingMemoryVerification }`. Field names mirror the spec exactly. `ExcludedMemory { result: BundleResult, exclusion_reason: String }` makes the \"and reasons\" half of the spec phrase a type-system requirement, not a convention.\n40\t4. Define supporting types in the same module: `Hypothesis { text, evidence_refs, confidence }`, `FailureRecord { kind, message, observed_at, evidence_refs }`, `PlanRef { plan_id, version }`, `BudgetDecisions { token_cap, dropped_count, truncated_results, pinned_identities }`, `WorkingMemoryVerification { last_verified_at, status: enum, notes }`.\n41\t5. Author the schema SQL in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/schema.sql` for the `working_memory_checkpoints` table: `(checkpoint_id INTEGER PK, workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL, session_id TEXT NOT NULL, task_id TEXT NOT NULL, checkpoint_name TEXT NOT NULL, created_at INTEGER NOT NULL, state_version INTEGER NOT NULL, state_json TEXT NOT NULL, state_hash TEXT NOT NULL)` plus indexes on `(workspace_id, session_id, task_id, created_at DESC)` and `(state_hash)`. `state_version` is bumped whenever `WorkingMemoryState` shape changes; migrations are rejected at load time if `state_version` is unknown.\n42\t6. Wire the migration into the existing storage bootstrap: `working_memory_checkpoints` lives in the existing memory DB (`.lattice/memories.db`) so it shares the session/task identity referenced elsewhere. Document this placement decision inline with `## Storage Design` citation.\n43\t7. Implement `save_checkpoint(state: &WorkingMemoryState, name: &str, conn: &Connection) -> Result<CheckpointId>` and `load_checkpoint(id: CheckpointId, conn: &Connection) -> Result<WorkingMemoryState>` in `state.rs`. Serialization uses serde JSON; `state_hash` is a deterministic SHA-256 over the canonical-JSON form so restore can be verified bit-for-bit.\n44\t8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state_tests.rs` covering: default-constructed state has the eleven required fields; serde round-trips the state without data loss; `save_checkpoint` followed by `load_checkpoint` returns a byte-identical `WorkingMemoryState`; `state_hash` matches between save and load; loading a checkpoint with an unknown `state_version` is rejected with a clear error; `excluded_memories` cannot be constructed without an `exclusion_reason` (type-system enforced).\n45\t9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n46\t\n47\t## Files expected\n48\t\n49\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs` — module skeleton re-exporting state, operations, event hooks.\n50\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` — `WorkingMemoryState` + supporting types + save/load checkpoint API.\n51\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/schema.sql` — `working_memory_checkpoints` table DDL and indexes.\n52\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for shape, serde round-trip, checkpoint save/load, state-version rejection.\n53\t\n54\t## Verification\n55\t\n56\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs`\n57\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs`\n58\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::state_tests`\n59\t\n60\t## Coding-standard checks\n61\t\n62\t- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n63\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Save/load are each their own function; serialization helpers extracted if `state.rs` approaches the cap.\n64\t- Schema parity: every column in `working_memory_checkpoints` has a corresponding `WorkingMemoryState` field or wrapper-record field; the `state_json` column mirrors the serde shape exactly. Schema doc and Rust struct are updated in the same commit.\n65\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n66\t- Single source of truth: identity types are reused from Phase 1; no parallel `FileId` or `SymbolId` definitions.\n67\t- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent; `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason` is non-optional.\n68\t- Doc citation: the state-field table cites `## 5. Working Memory`; the checkpoint table placement cites `## Storage Design` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n69\t\n70\t## Definition of done\n71\t\n72\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n73\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n74\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n75\t- [ ] No deferred work: every one of the eleven spec-named fields is in `WorkingMemoryState`; the `working_memory_checkpoints` table is created with versioned schema and deterministic hash.\n76\t- [ ] `excluded_memories` carries a typed `exclusion_reason` — the \"and reasons\" spec requirement is enforced by the type system, not by convention.\n77\t- [ ] Save/load round-trips a checkpoint byte-identically (regression test pinned).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2121c5-8450-4d0d-9f66-0986877cae23","uuid":"953783c3-ebf0-426b-9964-0e035e55dfaa","timestamp":"2026-05-17T10:13:14.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T34.md","content":"# T34 — Phase 5 — Working memory state model + working_memory_checkpoints table\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R33\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the per-task, short-lived working-memory state model the spec mandates in §5 — making context management explicit instead of implicit prompt accumulation — and pins it to a versioned `working_memory_checkpoints` SQLite table so checkpoints can be restored. The state model contains exactly the eleven fields the spec enumerates; the checkpoint schema preserves the full state along with timestamps and a checkpoint name so T35's `checkpoint` operation has a target to write into and T37's restore tests have a target to restore from.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Working memory is per-task and short-lived. It should be explicit rather than implicit prompt accumulation. Working memory contains: task statement; interpreted intent; active files and symbols; active hypotheses; active failures; current plan; selected memories; excluded memories and reasons; budget decisions; unresolved questions; verification status.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: explicit per-task working memory state; operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint; MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context; tests for token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - R33 verdict — Phase 4 retrieval is complete; `RetrievalBundle` / `BundleResult` are stable and can be embedded under `selected_memories`/`excluded_memories`.\n  - T27 `IntentClassification` — populates `interpreted_intent`.\n  - T28 `ResolvedAnchor` set — populates `active_files_and_symbols` seeds.\n  - T31 `RetrievalBundle` — supplies `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories` (with reasons) verbatim per the Phase 4 forward-compatibility contract.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — SQLite connection conventions, migration helpers.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — for the `verification_status` enum reused under \"verification status\".\n  - Phase 1 identity (`IdentityResolver`) — every reference inside working memory uses a stable identity.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, schema parity); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references; project build commands).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §5. Working Memory and §Phase 5: Working Memory in full; copy the eleven-field state list verbatim into a doc comment at the top of `state.rs`.\n2. Create the module skeleton: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs` re-exports `state`, `operations` (T35), `event_hooks` (T36) and registers the module with `lib.rs`.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` with `WorkingMemoryState { task_statement: String, interpreted_intent: IntentClassification, active_files: BTreeSet<FileIdentity>, active_symbols: BTreeSet<SymbolIdentity>, active_hypotheses: Vec<Hypothesis>, active_failures: Vec<FailureRecord>, current_plan: Option<PlanRef>, selected_memories: Vec<BundleResult>, excluded_memories: Vec<ExcludedMemory>, budget_decisions: BudgetDecisions, unresolved_questions: Vec<String>, verification_status: WorkingMemoryVerification }`. Field names mirror the spec exactly. `ExcludedMemory { result: BundleResult, exclusion_reason: String }` makes the \"and reasons\" half of the spec phrase a type-system requirement, not a convention.\n4. Define supporting types in the same module: `Hypothesis { text, evidence_refs, confidence }`, `FailureRecord { kind, message, observed_at, evidence_refs }`, `PlanRef { plan_id, version }`, `BudgetDecisions { token_cap, dropped_count, truncated_results, pinned_identities }`, `WorkingMemoryVerification { last_verified_at, status: enum, notes }`.\n5. Author the schema SQL in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/schema.sql` for the `working_memory_checkpoints` table: `(checkpoint_id INTEGER PK, workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL, session_id TEXT NOT NULL, task_id TEXT NOT NULL, checkpoint_name TEXT NOT NULL, created_at INTEGER NOT NULL, state_version INTEGER NOT NULL, state_json TEXT NOT NULL, state_hash TEXT NOT NULL)` plus indexes on `(workspace_id, session_id, task_id, created_at DESC)` and `(state_hash)`. `state_version` is bumped whenever `WorkingMemoryState` shape changes; migrations are rejected at load time if `state_version` is unknown.\n6. Wire the migration into the existing storage bootstrap: `working_memory_checkpoints` lives in the existing memory DB (`.lattice/memories.db`) so it shares the session/task identity referenced elsewhere. Document this placement decision inline with `## Storage Design` citation.\n7. Implement `save_checkpoint(state: &WorkingMemoryState, name: &str, conn: &Connection) -> Result<CheckpointId>` and `load_checkpoint(id: CheckpointId, conn: &Connection) -> Result<WorkingMemoryState>` in `state.rs`. Serialization uses serde JSON; `state_hash` is a deterministic SHA-256 over the canonical-JSON form so restore can be verified bit-for-bit.\n8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state_tests.rs` covering: default-constructed state has the eleven required fields; serde round-trips the state without data loss; `save_checkpoint` followed by `load_checkpoint` returns a byte-identical `WorkingMemoryState`; `state_hash` matches between save and load; loading a checkpoint with an unknown `state_version` is rejected with a clear error; `excluded_memories` cannot be constructed without an `exclusion_reason` (type-system enforced).\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs` — module skeleton re-exporting state, operations, event hooks.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` — `WorkingMemoryState` + supporting types + save/load checkpoint API.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/schema.sql` — `working_memory_checkpoints` table DDL and indexes.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for shape, serde round-trip, checkpoint save/load, state-version rejection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs`\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::state_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Save/load are each their own function; serialization helpers extracted if `state.rs` approaches the cap.\n- Schema parity: every column in `working_memory_checkpoints` has a corresponding `WorkingMemoryState` field or wrapper-record field; the `state_json` column mirrors the serde shape exactly. Schema doc and Rust struct are updated in the same commit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: identity types are reused from Phase 1; no parallel `FileId` or `SymbolId` definitions.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent; `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason` is non-optional.\n- Doc citation: the state-field table cites `## 5. Working Memory`; the checkpoint table placement cites `## Storage Design` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every one of the eleven spec-named fields is in `WorkingMemoryState`; the `working_memory_checkpoints` table is created with versioned schema and deterministic hash.\n- [ ] `excluded_memories` carries a typed `exclusion_reason` — the \"and reasons\" spec requirement is enforced by the type system, not by convention.\n- [ ] Save/load round-trips a checkpoint byte-identically (regression test pinned).\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
