{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVSd9NPVNk4Muw7TEo11no","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T35 — Phase 5 — Working memory operations (retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint)\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 5\n4\t**Type:** backend\n5\t**Model class:** balanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T34\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task implements every required operation on `WorkingMemoryState` from spec §5: `retrieve`, `summarize`, `filter`, `pin`, `evict`, `expand`, `compress`, `checkpoint`. Each operation mutates state in a documented, auditable way and pairs with a contract: every operation that drops or skips a memory must record the result in `excluded_memories` with a reason so the working-memory inspector (T36) can show what was intentionally left out. The operations integrate with Phase 4 retrieval (`retrieve` calls into the Phase 4 pipeline, `compress` invokes the shaper's compression policy, `pin` supplies the pin set the shaper honors).\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint. Working memory is not durable by itself. Durable value is extracted through event-backed consolidation.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n17\t\n18\t> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n19\t\n20\t> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n21\t\n22\t## Inputs\n23\t\n24\t- Dependency outputs:\n25\t  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState`, `ExcludedMemory`, `BudgetDecisions`, checkpoint save/load.\n26\t  - T31 `RetrievalBundle` and `ShaperContext.pins` interface — `pin` and `compress` route through the shaper to keep behaviour consistent with Phase 4.\n27\t  - T30 `RankedCandidate` (for `expand`, which re-runs scoring against a wider candidate set).\n28\t- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n29\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` and `scoring.rs` — invoked by `retrieve`, `compress`, `expand`.\n30\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` (T34) — every operation takes `&mut WorkingMemoryState`.\n31\t- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (single source of truth — no parallel ranker or shaper in this module); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n32\t\n33\t## Steps\n34\t\n35\t1. Re-read spec §5. Working Memory \"Required operations\" list and §Phase 5 Definition of Done to fix the contract for each operation.\n36\t2. Define an `Operation` trait or `WorkingMemoryOp` enum in `operations.rs` documenting the eight operations with one match arm per operation, so adding a ninth requires a deliberate type-system change.\n37\t3. Implement each operation as a free function `pub fn <op>(state: &mut WorkingMemoryState, args: <Op>Args, ctx: &OpContext) -> Result<<Op>Outcome>`, ≤50 lines each:\n38\t   - `retrieve(state, args, ctx)`: invokes the Phase 4 pipeline (intent → anchors → candidates → scoring → shaper) and merges the returned `RetrievalBundle` into `state.selected_memories`; every dropped candidate during shaper compression is captured in `state.excluded_memories` with its exclusion reason.\n39\t   - `summarize(state, args, ctx)`: returns a compact `WorkingMemorySummary` view (task, intent label, active file count, selected/excluded counts, budget usage, top hypotheses) for MCP display and event capture.\n40\t   - `filter(state, predicate, ctx)`: removes selected memories that fail `predicate`; removed entries move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"filtered: <predicate description>\"`.\n41\t   - `pin(state, identities, ctx)`: adds identities to `state.budget_decisions.pinned_identities`; documented contract is that subsequent `compress` and shaper-driven trimming must not drop pinned identities.\n42\t   - `evict(state, identities, ctx)`: removes identities from `selected_memories`, records each in `excluded_memories` with reason `\"evicted: <caller reason>\"`; refuses to evict pinned identities unless `force=true`.\n43\t   - `expand(state, target, ctx)`: re-runs Phase 4 scoring against a widened candidate set centred on `target` (a `BundleResult` already in `selected_memories`) using its `expansion_handle`; new high-ranked candidates are appended to `selected_memories`.\n44\t   - `compress(state, budget, ctx)`: reuses the shaper's compression policy on `state.selected_memories`, honoring `pinned_identities`; dropped results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"compressed: budget=<n> tokens\"`.\n45\t   - `checkpoint(state, name, ctx)`: calls `state::save_checkpoint(state, name, conn)` and returns the `CheckpointId`.\n46\t4. Make every operation idempotent where the spec implies it: calling `pin` twice on the same identity is a no-op; `evict` on an absent identity returns `Ok` with a documented no-op outcome; `checkpoint` with the same name versions the entry, never silently overwrites.\n47\t5. Wire `OpContext` so it carries the SQLite connection, retrieval profile, identity resolver, and shaper handle once — operations never construct these themselves.\n48\t6. Surface every state mutation through a single internal helper `record_state_mutation(state, op_name, before_hash, after_hash, summary)` so T36's event capture has a single hook to wire `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` events into.\n49\t7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` covering: each of the eight operations is exercised; `retrieve` populates both `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories`; `pin` then `compress` proves pinned identities survive; `evict` of a pinned identity without `force` is refused; `filter` records the predicate description; `summarize` returns a non-empty view with the expected fields; `expand` increases the selected-memories count when the candidate pool widens; `checkpoint` returns an id whose `load_checkpoint` byte-matches the state.\n50\t8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n51\t\n52\t## Files expected\n53\t\n54\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs` — eight operations, `OpContext`, internal state-mutation hook.\n55\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for every operation, pin/evict interaction, summarize, expand, checkpoint round-trip.\n56\t\n57\t## Verification\n58\t\n59\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`\n60\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::operations_tests`\n61\t\n62\t## Coding-standard checks\n63\t\n64\t- File length ≤800 lines per file. If `operations.rs` approaches the cap, split per-operation modules under `operations/` along operation boundaries.\n65\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each operation is its own function; the internal mutation hook is shared.\n66\t- Schema parity: any state mutation that needs persistence (only `checkpoint`) goes through T34's `save_checkpoint`; no parallel write path.\n67\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n68\t- Single source of truth: retrieval calls Phase 4 (`retrieval_v1::shaper`, `scoring`); no parallel candidate or scoring code here.\n69\t- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every operation name expresses intent; every drop/skip path writes to `excluded_memories` with a reason.\n70\t- Doc citation: each operation doc comment cites `## 5. Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n71\t\n72\t## Definition of done\n73\t\n74\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n75\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n76\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n77\t- [ ] No deferred work: all eight operations implemented; pin/evict/compress interaction enforced; `excluded_memories` populated by every drop/skip path.\n78\t- [ ] Idempotency contracts (pin, evict, checkpoint name versioning) covered by tests.\n79\t- [ ] `record_state_mutation` hook is in place ready for T36 to attach `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` event emission.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2121c5-8450-4d0d-9f66-0986877cae23","uuid":"c5ff9c93-69b1-401e-869b-36fd4aa8f4c4","timestamp":"2026-05-17T10:13:16.013Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md","content":"# T35 — Phase 5 — Working memory operations (retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint)\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T34\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements every required operation on `WorkingMemoryState` from spec §5: `retrieve`, `summarize`, `filter`, `pin`, `evict`, `expand`, `compress`, `checkpoint`. Each operation mutates state in a documented, auditable way and pairs with a contract: every operation that drops or skips a memory must record the result in `excluded_memories` with a reason so the working-memory inspector (T36) can show what was intentionally left out. The operations integrate with Phase 4 retrieval (`retrieve` calls into the Phase 4 pipeline, `compress` invokes the shaper's compression policy, `pin` supplies the pin set the shaper honors).\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint. Working memory is not durable by itself. Durable value is extracted through event-backed consolidation.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState`, `ExcludedMemory`, `BudgetDecisions`, checkpoint save/load.\n  - T31 `RetrievalBundle` and `ShaperContext.pins` interface — `pin` and `compress` route through the shaper to keep behaviour consistent with Phase 4.\n  - T30 `RankedCandidate` (for `expand`, which re-runs scoring against a wider candidate set).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` and `scoring.rs` — invoked by `retrieve`, `compress`, `expand`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` (T34) — every operation takes `&mut WorkingMemoryState`.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (single source of truth — no parallel ranker or shaper in this module); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §5. Working Memory \"Required operations\" list and §Phase 5 Definition of Done to fix the contract for each operation.\n2. Define an `Operation` trait or `WorkingMemoryOp` enum in `operations.rs` documenting the eight operations with one match arm per operation, so adding a ninth requires a deliberate type-system change.\n3. Implement each operation as a free function `pub fn <op>(state: &mut WorkingMemoryState, args: <Op>Args, ctx: &OpContext) -> Result<<Op>Outcome>`, ≤50 lines each:\n   - `retrieve(state, args, ctx)`: invokes the Phase 4 pipeline (intent → anchors → candidates → scoring → shaper) and merges the returned `RetrievalBundle` into `state.selected_memories`; every dropped candidate during shaper compression is captured in `state.excluded_memories` with its exclusion reason.\n   - `summarize(state, args, ctx)`: returns a compact `WorkingMemorySummary` view (task, intent label, active file count, selected/excluded counts, budget usage, top hypotheses) for MCP display and event capture.\n   - `filter(state, predicate, ctx)`: removes selected memories that fail `predicate`; removed entries move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"filtered: <predicate description>\"`.\n   - `pin(state, identities, ctx)`: adds identities to `state.budget_decisions.pinned_identities`; documented contract is that subsequent `compress` and shaper-driven trimming must not drop pinned identities.\n   - `evict(state, identities, ctx)`: removes identities from `selected_memories`, records each in `excluded_memories` with reason `\"evicted: <caller reason>\"`; refuses to evict pinned identities unless `force=true`.\n   - `expand(state, target, ctx)`: re-runs Phase 4 scoring against a widened candidate set centred on `target` (a `BundleResult` already in `selected_memories`) using its `expansion_handle`; new high-ranked candidates are appended to `selected_memories`.\n   - `compress(state, budget, ctx)`: reuses the shaper's compression policy on `state.selected_memories`, honoring `pinned_identities`; dropped results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"compressed: budget=<n> tokens\"`.\n   - `checkpoint(state, name, ctx)`: calls `state::save_checkpoint(state, name, conn)` and returns the `CheckpointId`.\n4. Make every operation idempotent where the spec implies it: calling `pin` twice on the same identity is a no-op; `evict` on an absent identity returns `Ok` with a documented no-op outcome; `checkpoint` with the same name versions the entry, never silently overwrites.\n5. Wire `OpContext` so it carries the SQLite connection, retrieval profile, identity resolver, and shaper handle once — operations never construct these themselves.\n6. Surface every state mutation through a single internal helper `record_state_mutation(state, op_name, before_hash, after_hash, summary)` so T36's event capture has a single hook to wire `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` events into.\n7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` covering: each of the eight operations is exercised; `retrieve` populates both `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories`; `pin` then `compress` proves pinned identities survive; `evict` of a pinned identity without `force` is refused; `filter` records the predicate description; `summarize` returns a non-empty view with the expected fields; `expand` increases the selected-memories count when the candidate pool widens; `checkpoint` returns an id whose `load_checkpoint` byte-matches the state.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs` — eight operations, `OpContext`, internal state-mutation hook.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for every operation, pin/evict interaction, summarize, expand, checkpoint round-trip.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::operations_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If `operations.rs` approaches the cap, split per-operation modules under `operations/` along operation boundaries.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each operation is its own function; the internal mutation hook is shared.\n- Schema parity: any state mutation that needs persistence (only `checkpoint`) goes through T34's `save_checkpoint`; no parallel write path.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: retrieval calls Phase 4 (`retrieval_v1::shaper`, `scoring`); no parallel candidate or scoring code here.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every operation name expresses intent; every drop/skip path writes to `excluded_memories` with a reason.\n- Doc citation: each operation doc comment cites `## 5. Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all eight operations implemented; pin/evict/compress interaction enforced; `excluded_memories` populated by every drop/skip path.\n- [ ] Idempotency contracts (pin, evict, checkpoint name versioning) covered by tests.\n- [ ] `record_state_mutation` hook is in place ready for T36 to attach `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` event emission.\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":80}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Gox9BGui3zEmqQ1JgfCif4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019fHmZUqgiF3qJJket5ULY5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T36.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_read_input_tokens":82282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1389},"output_tokens":71,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2121c5-8450-4d0d-9f66-0986877cae23","uuid":"96b60346-6a68-4719-a23e-4d875d123cc0","request_id":"req_011Cb7xpnFnihaQVrDZ9rrFV"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019fHmZUqgiF3qJJket5ULY5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T36 — Phase 5 — MCP surface for working memory inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 5\n4\t**Type:** backend\n5\t**Model class:** balanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T34, T35\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task delivers the MCP tool that lets a client inspect the current `WorkingMemoryState` and the event-capture hooks that automatically log included and excluded context per spec §Phase 5 deliverable (\"automatic event capture for included and excluded context\"). The MCP tool exposes the same compact-by-default shape the rest of the MCP surface uses; the event hooks emit `MemoryRetrieved` and `MemoryExpanded` events (Phase 2 event kinds) every time the working memory's `selected_memories` or `excluded_memories` change. Together these make working memory observable — meeting the Phase 5 Definition of Done (\"workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded\").\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n17\t\n18\t> \"Required event types: ... ContextBundleReturned; MemoryRetrieved; MemoryExpanded ...\" (spec §3. Event Log)\n19\t\n20\t> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n21\t\n22\t> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering; full structured JSON; context handles; stable expansion targets; budget controls.\" (spec §9. MCP Surface)\n23\t\n24\t## Inputs\n25\t\n26\t- Dependency outputs:\n27\t  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState` and checkpoint API.\n28\t  - T35 `OpContext`, eight operations, and `record_state_mutation` internal hook.\n29\t  - Phase 2 event-log API — exposes `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `ContextBundleReturned` writers.\n30\t- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n31\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server registration.\n32\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — `McpHandler::handle_tools_call()` dispatch and tool-schema declarations.\n33\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — context-handle convention for round-trippable handles.\n34\t  - Phase 2 event writer (assumed to live at `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/`).\n35\t- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, single source of truth — reuse the existing MCP dispatch convention); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (compact-by-default; build/deploy procedure for the daemon).\n36\t\n37\t## Steps\n38\t\n39\t1. Re-read spec §Phase 5 deliverables, §3. Event Log event-kind list, and §9. MCP Surface response contract to fix the tool shape and event-emission contract.\n40\t2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`: register a new MCP tool `inspect_working_memory` with schema `{ task_id: string, mode: \"compact\" | \"diagnostic\", include_excluded: boolean }`. The handler loads the active `WorkingMemoryState` for the task (from the session-scoped in-memory store maintained by T35's `OpContext`, falling back to the latest checkpoint if the session has rolled), then returns either a compact summary (via T35 `summarize`) or the full state including `excluded_memories` when `include_excluded=true`. Response carries an `expansion_handle` per spec §9 so the caller can expand the full state without re-fetching.\n41\t3. Wire the tool into `mcp.rs` dispatch alongside the existing 43 tools. Tool registration includes the schema in the MCP `tools/list` response; failure to expose a parameter is a contract violation caught by the cross-layer MCP schema test gate.\n42\t4. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs`: a small module exposing `emit_memory_retrieved(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)` and `emit_memory_expanded(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)`. Each function computes the diff (which identities were added to `selected_memories`, which were added to `excluded_memories` with reasons), packages the diff into an event payload per Phase 2's event-payload contract (workspace, branch, session, task, actor, timestamp, payload hash, compact summary, optional full payload location), and writes through the Phase 2 event writer.\n43\t5. Attach the hooks to T35's `record_state_mutation` so every state-mutating operation emits the appropriate event automatically: `retrieve` and `compress` emit `MemoryRetrieved` (since they decide what is included/excluded); `expand` emits `MemoryExpanded`; `pin`, `evict`, `filter`, `checkpoint` emit `MemoryRetrieved` when they change inclusion/exclusion. `summarize` emits no event.\n44\t6. Honor the spec invariant \"the full event stream should not be injected into prompts\" — the event hooks never put event data back into `WorkingMemoryState`. Events flow one way: state mutation → event log.\n45\t7. Hot-path discipline: event writes share the existing Phase 2 write budget (`≤5ms P99`). If the writer returns a backpressure error, the operation does not fail — the event is dropped with a `warn!` log naming the task and operation, per `coding.md` \"no silent .catch\" but tolerant of event-log overload.\n46\t8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` covering: tool registration appears in `tools/list`; compact mode returns a summary; diagnostic mode returns the full state and embedded `RetrievalBundle`-shaped `selected_memories`; `include_excluded=true` returns excluded entries with reasons; expansion handle round-trips back to the same state; a synthetic event writer captures one `MemoryRetrieved` event per `retrieve` call and one `MemoryExpanded` event per `expand` call; event payload carries the included and excluded identity diffs and reasons.\n47\t9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` (release build verifies the whole daemon still compiles with the new tool registered), then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`. Deploy the new daemon binary per the project rule (`pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`) only when explicitly told to ship; the test commands themselves do not require a redeploy.\n48\t\n49\t## Files expected\n50\t\n51\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` — MCP tool registration, schema, handler, dispatch wiring.\n52\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs` — `emit_memory_retrieved`, `emit_memory_expanded`, state-diff computation, event payload assembly.\n53\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, event capture.\n54\t\n55\t## Verification\n56\t\n57\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`\n58\t- `cd daemon && cargo build --release`\n59\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`\n60\t\n61\t## Coding-standard checks\n62\t\n63\t- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n64\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. The MCP handler decomposes mode handling into helpers; event-diff computation is its own function.\n65\t- Schema parity: the MCP tool JSON schema mirrors the Rust handler's parameter struct exactly; the response shape mirrors `WorkingMemoryState` (compact view exposes a documented subset). Schema declaration and Rust struct are updated in the same commit.\n66\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n67\t- Single source of truth: state loading uses T34's `load_checkpoint` / T35's `OpContext` session store; no parallel state lookup. Event writing uses the Phase 2 event writer; no parallel event payload assembler.\n68\t- No broken windows: dead imports removed; the backpressure-drop path logs at `warn!` with task and operation context, never silent.\n69\t- Doc citation: tool comments cite `## 9. MCP Surface`; event-hook comments cite `## 3. Event Log` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n70\t\n71\t## Definition of done\n72\t\n73\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n74\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n75\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n76\t- [ ] No deferred work: tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, automatic event capture all delivered in this task.\n77\t- [ ] Every Phase-5 state mutation emits an event without manual call sites — the `record_state_mutation` hook is the single attachment point.\n78\t- [ ] Backpressure on the event log degrades to a logged drop, not a failed operation.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2121c5-8450-4d0d-9f66-0986877cae23","uuid":"b14c0456-8fb5-4fdd-b03a-159544cd43e3","timestamp":"2026-05-17T10:13:17.133Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T36.md","content":"# T36 — Phase 5 — MCP surface for working memory inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T34, T35\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the MCP tool that lets a client inspect the current `WorkingMemoryState` and the event-capture hooks that automatically log included and excluded context per spec §Phase 5 deliverable (\"automatic event capture for included and excluded context\"). The MCP tool exposes the same compact-by-default shape the rest of the MCP surface uses; the event hooks emit `MemoryRetrieved` and `MemoryExpanded` events (Phase 2 event kinds) every time the working memory's `selected_memories` or `excluded_memories` change. Together these make working memory observable — meeting the Phase 5 Definition of Done (\"workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded\").\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Required event types: ... ContextBundleReturned; MemoryRetrieved; MemoryExpanded ...\" (spec §3. Event Log)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering; full structured JSON; context handles; stable expansion targets; budget controls.\" (spec §9. MCP Surface)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState` and checkpoint API.\n  - T35 `OpContext`, eight operations, and `record_state_mutation` internal hook.\n  - Phase 2 event-log API — exposes `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `ContextBundleReturned` writers.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server registration.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — `McpHandler::handle_tools_call()` dispatch and tool-schema declarations.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — context-handle convention for round-trippable handles.\n  - Phase 2 event writer (assumed to live at `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/`).\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, single source of truth — reuse the existing MCP dispatch convention); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (compact-by-default; build/deploy procedure for the daemon).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §Phase 5 deliverables, §3. Event Log event-kind list, and §9. MCP Surface response contract to fix the tool shape and event-emission contract.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`: register a new MCP tool `inspect_working_memory` with schema `{ task_id: string, mode: \"compact\" | \"diagnostic\", include_excluded: boolean }`. The handler loads the active `WorkingMemoryState` for the task (from the session-scoped in-memory store maintained by T35's `OpContext`, falling back to the latest checkpoint if the session has rolled), then returns either a compact summary (via T35 `summarize`) or the full state including `excluded_memories` when `include_excluded=true`. Response carries an `expansion_handle` per spec §9 so the caller can expand the full state without re-fetching.\n3. Wire the tool into `mcp.rs` dispatch alongside the existing 43 tools. Tool registration includes the schema in the MCP `tools/list` response; failure to expose a parameter is a contract violation caught by the cross-layer MCP schema test gate.\n4. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs`: a small module exposing `emit_memory_retrieved(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)` and `emit_memory_expanded(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)`. Each function computes the diff (which identities were added to `selected_memories`, which were added to `excluded_memories` with reasons), packages the diff into an event payload per Phase 2's event-payload contract (workspace, branch, session, task, actor, timestamp, payload hash, compact summary, optional full payload location), and writes through the Phase 2 event writer.\n5. Attach the hooks to T35's `record_state_mutation` so every state-mutating operation emits the appropriate event automatically: `retrieve` and `compress` emit `MemoryRetrieved` (since they decide what is included/excluded); `expand` emits `MemoryExpanded`; `pin`, `evict`, `filter`, `checkpoint` emit `MemoryRetrieved` when they change inclusion/exclusion. `summarize` emits no event.\n6. Honor the spec invariant \"the full event stream should not be injected into prompts\" — the event hooks never put event data back into `WorkingMemoryState`. Events flow one way: state mutation → event log.\n7. Hot-path discipline: event writes share the existing Phase 2 write budget (`≤5ms P99`). If the writer returns a backpressure error, the operation does not fail — the event is dropped with a `warn!` log naming the task and operation, per `coding.md` \"no silent .catch\" but tolerant of event-log overload.\n8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` covering: tool registration appears in `tools/list`; compact mode returns a summary; diagnostic mode returns the full state and embedded `RetrievalBundle`-shaped `selected_memories`; `include_excluded=true` returns excluded entries with reasons; expansion handle round-trips back to the same state; a synthetic event writer captures one `MemoryRetrieved` event per `retrieve` call and one `MemoryExpanded` event per `expand` call; event payload carries the included and excluded identity diffs and reasons.\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` (release build verifies the whole daemon still compiles with the new tool registered), then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`. Deploy the new daemon binary per the project rule (`pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`) only when explicitly told to ship; the test commands themselves do not require a redeploy.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` — MCP tool registration, schema, handler, dispatch wiring.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs` — `emit_memory_retrieved`, `emit_memory_expanded`, state-diff computation, event payload assembly.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, event capture.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. The MCP handler decomposes mode handling into helpers; event-diff computation is its own function.\n- Schema parity: the MCP tool JSON schema mirrors the Rust handler's parameter struct exactly; the response shape mirrors `WorkingMemoryState` (compact view exposes a documented subset). Schema declaration and Rust struct are updated in the same commit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: state loading uses T34's `load_checkpoint` / T35's `OpContext` session store; no parallel state lookup. Event writing uses the Phase 2 event writer; no parallel event payload assembler.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed; the backpressure-drop path logs at `warn!` with task and operation context, never silent.\n- Doc citation: tool comments cite `## 9. MCP Surface`; event-hook comments cite `## 3. Event Log` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, automatic event capture all delivered in this task.\n- [ ] Every Phase-5 state mutation emits an event without manual call sites — the `record_state_mutation` hook is the single attachment point.\n- [ ] Backpressure on the event log degrades to a logged drop, not a failed operation.\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
