{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PGnjkj5cKcXH9rDLQb1ZJL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T37 — Phase 5 — Working memory tests (budgets, pins, eviction, checkpoint restore)\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 5\n4\t**Type:** tests\n5\t**Model class:** balanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T34, T35, T36\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task closes Phase 5 with the four test families spec §Phase 5 names explicitly: token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore. Each family lives in its own in-tree test module so failures map directly to the spec deliverable they regress. The tests are end-to-end across T34 (state model), T35 (operations), and T36 (event capture) so a failure surfaces wherever the contract broke, not only at the unit boundary.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... tests for token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n17\t\n18\t> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n19\t\n20\t> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n21\t\n22\t## Inputs\n23\t\n24\t- Dependency outputs:\n25\t  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState`, `BudgetDecisions`, checkpoint save/load.\n26\t  - T35 eight operations and `OpContext`.\n27\t  - T36 event hooks (so tests can assert event emissions when relevant).\n28\t- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n29\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/` (modules under test).\n30\t  - Synthetic fixture helpers (small workspace, small candidate set) developed alongside the Phase 4 tests in T32 — reused so fixtures are not duplicated.\n31\t- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (tests as documentation: one test per behaviour, ≤30 lines per test, named for the behaviour); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n32\t\n33\t## Steps\n34\t\n35\t1. Re-read spec §Phase 5 Deliverables to fix the exact test families required; each family has its own file.\n36\t2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs` covering: `compress` honors `budget_decisions.token_cap`; over-budget retrieval truncates and sets `BudgetReport::truncated = true`; truncated results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"compressed: budget=<n> tokens\"`; budget changes between operations affect only subsequent operations, not retroactively; a synthetic huge candidate set respects per-source caps so working memory never grows unbounded.\n37\t3. Implement pinned-context regression tests inside `budget_tests.rs` (or split into a small `pin_tests` if file size demands): `pin` makes an identity survive `compress`; `pin` twice on the same identity is idempotent; `evict` on a pinned identity without `force=true` is refused with a clear error; `evict` with `force=true` records the pinned identity in `excluded_memories` with reason naming the force; pin survives `checkpoint`/`load_checkpoint` round-trip.\n38\t4. Implement eviction regression tests in `budget_tests.rs` (or split): `evict` of a present identity moves it to `excluded_memories` with the caller-supplied reason; `evict` of an absent identity returns Ok with a documented no-op outcome; `evict` does not emit an event when nothing changed (T36 hook respects no-op); `evict` followed by `retrieve` for the same identity re-includes it (eviction is not a permanent deny-list within a session).\n39\t5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs` covering: `checkpoint` returns a `CheckpointId` whose `load_checkpoint` produces a byte-identical state (verified via canonical-JSON SHA-256); two checkpoints with the same name produce distinct ids and both round-trip; loading an unknown checkpoint id returns a typed error; loading a checkpoint whose `state_version` is newer than the running daemon is rejected with a clear error; restoring a checkpoint resets `selected_memories`, `excluded_memories`, and `budget_decisions` together (they are coherent state, never restored partially).\n40\t6. Each test is ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\"; setup is extracted into helpers when the assertion would otherwise share lines with setup.\n41\t7. Run both verification test commands; if any test depends on a fixture not built by T32, build the minimal helper in a `tests_common.rs` sibling (no duplicated workspace generation in two places).\n42\t8. Audit the entire file set for the standard `coding.md` violations (TODOs, suppressions, commented-out code, dead imports); fix in this same commit before stopping.\n43\t\n44\t## Files expected\n45\t\n46\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs` — token-budget, pinned-context, eviction regression tests.\n47\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs` — checkpoint save/load, byte-identical restore, unknown-id and version-rejection tests.\n48\t\n49\t## Verification\n50\t\n51\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs`\n52\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs`\n53\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::budget_tests`\n54\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::checkpoint_tests`\n55\t\n56\t## Coding-standard checks\n57\t\n58\t- File length ≤800 lines per file. If `budget_tests.rs` approaches the cap when pinned-context and eviction sit alongside budgets, split into `pin_tests.rs` and `eviction_tests.rs` (each registered under `working_memory/mod.rs`) rather than letting one file exceed the cap.\n59\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each test ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\".\n60\t- Schema parity: tests use the canonical `WorkingMemoryState` and `BudgetDecisions` types from T34; no parallel test-only state struct.\n61\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n62\t- Single source of truth: fixture helpers shared with T32 or extracted into a sibling test-common module; fixtures are not duplicated.\n63\t- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every test is named for the behaviour it asserts (e.g. `test_pin_survives_compress`, `test_checkpoint_round_trip_byte_identical`).\n64\t- Doc citation: test-module head comments cite `## Phase 5: Working Memory` and `## 5. Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n65\t\n66\t## Definition of done\n67\t\n68\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n69\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n70\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n71\t- [ ] No deferred work: all four spec-named test families (budgets, pinned context, eviction, checkpoint restore) covered.\n72\t- [ ] Pin/evict/force interaction has a regression test that surfaces violations clearly.\n73\t- [ ] Checkpoint round-trip is byte-identical (canonical-JSON SHA-256 verified).\n74\t- [ ] Eviction is non-permanent within a session (retrieve re-includes); regression pinned.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2121c5-8450-4d0d-9f66-0986877cae23","uuid":"3a317bdc-d13e-49d6-b54b-d58637f35ce9","timestamp":"2026-05-17T10:13:17.335Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T37.md","content":"# T37 — Phase 5 — Working memory tests (budgets, pins, eviction, checkpoint restore)\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T34, T35, T36\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task closes Phase 5 with the four test families spec §Phase 5 names explicitly: token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore. Each family lives in its own in-tree test module so failures map directly to the spec deliverable they regress. The tests are end-to-end across T34 (state model), T35 (operations), and T36 (event capture) so a failure surfaces wherever the contract broke, not only at the unit boundary.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... tests for token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState`, `BudgetDecisions`, checkpoint save/load.\n  - T35 eight operations and `OpContext`.\n  - T36 event hooks (so tests can assert event emissions when relevant).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/` (modules under test).\n  - Synthetic fixture helpers (small workspace, small candidate set) developed alongside the Phase 4 tests in T32 — reused so fixtures are not duplicated.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (tests as documentation: one test per behaviour, ≤30 lines per test, named for the behaviour); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §Phase 5 Deliverables to fix the exact test families required; each family has its own file.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs` covering: `compress` honors `budget_decisions.token_cap`; over-budget retrieval truncates and sets `BudgetReport::truncated = true`; truncated results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"compressed: budget=<n> tokens\"`; budget changes between operations affect only subsequent operations, not retroactively; a synthetic huge candidate set respects per-source caps so working memory never grows unbounded.\n3. Implement pinned-context regression tests inside `budget_tests.rs` (or split into a small `pin_tests` if file size demands): `pin` makes an identity survive `compress`; `pin` twice on the same identity is idempotent; `evict` on a pinned identity without `force=true` is refused with a clear error; `evict` with `force=true` records the pinned identity in `excluded_memories` with reason naming the force; pin survives `checkpoint`/`load_checkpoint` round-trip.\n4. Implement eviction regression tests in `budget_tests.rs` (or split): `evict` of a present identity moves it to `excluded_memories` with the caller-supplied reason; `evict` of an absent identity returns Ok with a documented no-op outcome; `evict` does not emit an event when nothing changed (T36 hook respects no-op); `evict` followed by `retrieve` for the same identity re-includes it (eviction is not a permanent deny-list within a session).\n5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs` covering: `checkpoint` returns a `CheckpointId` whose `load_checkpoint` produces a byte-identical state (verified via canonical-JSON SHA-256); two checkpoints with the same name produce distinct ids and both round-trip; loading an unknown checkpoint id returns a typed error; loading a checkpoint whose `state_version` is newer than the running daemon is rejected with a clear error; restoring a checkpoint resets `selected_memories`, `excluded_memories`, and `budget_decisions` together (they are coherent state, never restored partially).\n6. Each test is ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\"; setup is extracted into helpers when the assertion would otherwise share lines with setup.\n7. Run both verification test commands; if any test depends on a fixture not built by T32, build the minimal helper in a `tests_common.rs` sibling (no duplicated workspace generation in two places).\n8. Audit the entire file set for the standard `coding.md` violations (TODOs, suppressions, commented-out code, dead imports); fix in this same commit before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs` — token-budget, pinned-context, eviction regression tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs` — checkpoint save/load, byte-identical restore, unknown-id and version-rejection tests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs`\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/checkpoint_tests.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::budget_tests`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::checkpoint_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If `budget_tests.rs` approaches the cap when pinned-context and eviction sit alongside budgets, split into `pin_tests.rs` and `eviction_tests.rs` (each registered under `working_memory/mod.rs`) rather than letting one file exceed the cap.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each test ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\".\n- Schema parity: tests use the canonical `WorkingMemoryState` and `BudgetDecisions` types from T34; no parallel test-only state struct.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: fixture helpers shared with T32 or extracted into a sibling test-common module; fixtures are not duplicated.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every test is named for the behaviour it asserts (e.g. `test_pin_survives_compress`, `test_checkpoint_round_trip_byte_identical`).\n- Doc citation: test-module head comments cite `## Phase 5: Working Memory` and `## 5. Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all four spec-named test families (budgets, pinned context, eviction, checkpoint restore) covered.\n- [ ] Pin/evict/force interaction has a regression test that surfaces violations clearly.\n- [ ] Checkpoint round-trip is byte-identical (canonical-JSON SHA-256 verified).\n- [ ] Eviction is non-permanent within a session (retrieve re-includes); regression pinned.\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":75}}}
